==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|k|u}}

===Etymology===
Possibly from {{etyl|urj-pro|fi}} {{recons|kumpa||wave|lang=urj-pro}}, whence also eg. Hungarian {{term|hab||foam|lang=hu}}. {{etyl|gem|fi}} origin is also possible, cf. Proto-Germanic {{recons|humpaz|lang=gem-pro}} (whence English {{term|hump|lang=en}}).

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# A [[hummock]], [[hillock]] (small natural elevation of earth, generally smaller than {{term|kukkula||hill}}, larger than {{term|kumpare||knoll}}).
# A [[mound]] (small, rounded, artificial elevation of earth).

